//? Title: KMP matching through actual byte comparisons
//? Subtitle: Prefix borders, overlapping matches and measured fallback work
//? Exports: both
//? Lang: en-GB

\abstract(
Exact matching must find every occurrence of a byte pattern in a text, including
overlaps, without rescanning the text from each candidate start. KMP reuses the
pattern’s own prefix/suffix structure to preserve earlier evidence after a
mismatch. We retain the original ababaca prefix example and both original
searches, inspect actual producing comparison operands, and measure a linear
selected-work bound on repetitive adversarial inputs. Empty-needle and
embedded-NUL controls state the byte-level contract explicitly.
)

\toc

> Borders explain the fallback

For a pattern P, pi[i] is the largest proper-prefix length that is also a suffix
of P[0..i]. “Proper” means pi[i]<=i; pi[0]=0. After matching q bytes, a mismatch
can only preserve a border of that matched prefix: replace q by pi[q−1],
repeating until extension succeeds or q reaches zero. Text position never
decreases, though the same byte can be compared more than once.

The native implementation deliberately retains its original while-then-if order.
A positive-border while test compares bytes even when equal; the following
extension if can test that same equal pair again. Counters and records count
both actual comparisons. A full match resets q to its longest border so
overlapping occurrences survive. Bytes are compared exactly, without Unicode
normalization or code-point interpretation. The historical empty-pattern
convention is no matches, and a pattern longer than text exits before
constructing pi.

> See the original failure links

For ababaca the prefix table is0,0,1,2,3,0,1. At position5 the new c cannot
extend either the three-byte or one-byte border. The diagram uses actual
prefix-phase while-mismatch records produced during a complete search, not a
separately simulated automaton.

```{cpp, results="markdown", file="figures/kmp_fallback.svg", flags="-std=c++23 -O2 $(pkg-config --cflags --libs datamunge) -Wl,-rpath,$(pkg-config --variable=libdir datamunge)"}
#include <dm/dm.hpp>
int main() {
    std::filesystem::create_directories("build");
    const auto t =
        dm::algorithms::kmp_search_trace("ababacaababaca", "ababaca");
    dm::graphics::Diagram d;
    std::size_t count = 0;
    std::print("| actual pattern index | tested border | source byte | pattern byte | equality |\n| ---: | " "---: | ---: | ---: | --- |\n");
    for (const auto &e : t.comparisons)
        if (e.phase == dm::algorithms::KMPPhase::Prefix &&
            e.site == dm::algorithms::KMPSite::While && !e.equal) {
            std::print("| {} | {} | {} | {} | {} |\n", e.index, e.border,
                       unsigned(e.source_byte), unsigned(e.pattern_byte),
                       e.equal);
    const auto id = std::to_string(count);
    d.node(id, {double(count) * 6, 0},
           std::format("Actual pattern index {}\nborder {} mismatches byte {}",
                       e.index, e.border, unsigned(e.source_byte)));
    if (count)
        d.edge(std::to_string(count - 1), id);
    ++count;
        }
        std::print("\nActual prefix comparisons {}; actual prefix fallbacks {}.\n",
                   t.work.prefix_comparisons, t.work.prefix_fallbacks);
        d.save_svg("build/kmp_fallback.svg");
}
```
