> Original prefix table and both original searches

The two complete searches use ababacaababaca with needle ababaca, and ababababa
with needle aba. The first has starts0 and7; the second preserves overlaps
at0,2,4,6. Reported starts are original byte offsets. Prefix construction is
part of each actual search’s selected work; the standalone prefix API returns
the same table on a nonempty valid search.

```{cpp, results="markdown", file="figures/kmp_original.svg", flags="-std=c++23 -O2 $(pkg-config --cflags --libs datamunge) -Wl,-rpath,$(pkg-config --variable=libdir datamunge)"}
#include <dm/dm.hpp>
int main() {
    std::filesystem::create_directories("build");
    const std::string pattern = "ababaca";
    const auto pi = dm::algorithms::kmp_prefix_function(pattern);
    std::vector<double> x, y;
    std::print("| original pattern index | byte | actual prefix length |\n| ---: | ---: | ---: |\n");
    for (std::size_t i = 0; i < pi.size(); ++i) {
        std::print("| {} | {} | {} |\n", i, pattern[i], pi[i]);
        x.push_back(i);
        y.push_back(pi[i]);
    }
    std::print("\n| original text | original needle | actual match start |\n| --- | --- | ---: |\n");
    for (const auto & [text, needle] : std::vector<std::pair<std::string, std::string>> {
        { "ababacaababaca", "ababaca" }, {"ababababa", "aba"}
    }) {
        const auto t = dm::algorithms::kmp_search_trace(text, needle);
        for (auto i : t.matches)
            std::print("| {} | {} | {} |\n", text, needle, i);
    }
    auto p = dm::graphics::RPlot::create();
    p.bars(x, y, "pi", {37, 99, 235}, .6).points(x, y, "", {220, 38, 38}, 5).y_limits(-.25, 4).title("Original ababaca: actual proper borders").x_label("original pattern byte index").y_label("actual prefix/suffix length").save_svg("build/kmp_original.svg");
}
```
