> Repeated comparisons and binary controls

A repeated text position is legitimate: fallback changes the candidate border
while preserving the current text byte. The plot shows actual original text
indices against text-phase comparison ordinal. This separates “the text cursor
never rewinds” from the false claim that each byte is tested exactly once.
Embedded NUL is an ordinary byte, and an empty needle follows the library’s
deliberate no-match convention.

```{cpp, results="markdown", file="figures/kmp_comparisons.svg", flags="-std=c++23 -O2 $(pkg-config --cflags --libs datamunge) -Wl,-rpath,$(pkg-config --variable=libdir datamunge)"}
#include <dm/dm.hpp>
int main() {
    std::filesystem::create_directories("build");
    const auto t = dm::algorithms::kmp_search_trace("aaaaac", "aaab");
    std::vector<double> x, y;
    std::print("| actual text test ordinal | original text index | tested border | equality | while site " "|\n| ---: | ---: | ---: | --- | --- |\n");
    for (const auto &e : t.comparisons)
        if (e.phase == dm::algorithms::KMPPhase::Text) {
            std::print("| {} | {} | {} | {} | {} |\n", x.size(), e.index,
                       e.border, e.equal,
                       e.site == dm::algorithms::KMPSite::While);
    x.push_back(x.size());
    y.push_back(e.index);
        }
        std::print("\n| control | actual occurrences |\n| --- | ---: |\n");
        std::print("| empty needle | {} |\n",
                   dm::algorithms::kmp_search("abc", "").size());
        std::print("| longer needle | {} |\n",
                   dm::algorithms::kmp_search("a", "aaa").size());
        std::print("| embedded NUL overlap | {} |\n",
                   dm::algorithms::kmp_search(std::string("a\0a\0a", 5),
                                              std::string("a\0a", 3)).size());
        auto p = dm::graphics::RPlot::create();
        p.line(x, y, "text index", {37, 99, 235}, 2).points(x, y, "",
                                                            {37, 99, 235}, 4).title("Actual comparisons can revisit the current byte").x_label("actual text comparison ordinal").y_label("original text byte index").save_svg("build/kmp_comparisons.svg");
}
```
