> Checking the linear work argument

Each mismatch fallback strictly decreases q, and only successful extensions
increase it. At most n extensions occur in a text scan, so there are at most n
mismatch fallbacks. At most one successful positive-border while test and one
final extension test occur per position. Consequently text comparisons<=3n for
this preserved implementation; prefix comparisons<=3(m−1) for m>0. These
conservative counts exclude integer branch tests, memory traffic, allocation,
output and time. Prefix construction and scanning take O(n+m) work; the table
uses O(m), with O(number of matches) output. Trace mode additionally owns inputs
and all actual records.

The following complete adversarial runs use text a repeated n−1 times then c,
with needle a repeated31 times then b. Count-only analysis shares the same
producer without storing an ever larger history. The plotted reference is the
proved comparison bound, not a fabricated measured growth curve.

```{cpp, results="markdown", file="figures/kmp_work.svg", flags="-std=c++23 -O2 $(pkg-config --cflags --libs datamunge) -Wl,-rpath,$(pkg-config --variable=libdir datamunge)"}
#include <dm/dm.hpp>
int main() {
    std::filesystem::create_directories("build");
    std::vector<double> x, y, b;
    const std::string pattern = std::string(31, 'a') + 'b';
    std::print("| actual text length | prefix comparisons | actual text comparisons | text fallbacks | " "conservative text bound | matches |\n| ---: | ---: | ---: | ---: | ---: | ---: |\n");
    for (std::size_t n : {64, 256, 1024, 4096, 16384}) {
        const auto a =
            dm::algorithms::kmp_search_analyze(std::string(n - 1, 'a') + 'c',
                                               pattern);
        std::print("| {} | {} | {} | {} | {} | {} |\n", n,
                   a.work.prefix_comparisons, a.work.text_comparisons,
                   a.work.text_fallbacks, 3 * n, a.matches.size());
        x.push_back(std::log2(n));
        y.push_back(std::log2(a.work.text_comparisons));
        b.push_back(std::log2(3 * n));
    }
    auto p = dm::graphics::RPlot::create();
    p.line(x, y, "actual", {37, 99, 235}, 2).points(x, y, "", {37, 99, 235}, 4).line(x, b, "bound", {220, 38, 38}, 2).title("Actual adversarial comparisons and the 3n bound").x_label("log2(actual text length)").y_label("log2(byte comparisons)").save_svg("build/kmp_work.svg");
}
```
// result_begin: markdown
| actual text length | prefix comparisons | actual text comparisons | text fallbacks | conservative text bound | matches |
