| 64 | 90 | 189 | 63 | 192 | 0 |
| 256 | 90 | 765 | 255 | 768 | 0 |
| 1024 | 90 | 3069 | 1023 | 3072 | 0 |
| 4096 | 90 | 12285 | 4095 | 12288 | 0 |
| 16384 | 90 | 49149 | 16383 | 49152 | 0 |
\image(figures/kmp_work.svg)
// result_end
\caption(Actual selected byte-comparison work versus the explicit conservative bound.)
\alttext(Complete count-only runs on repetitive adversarial inputs remain below the three-n bound; no elapsed-time claim is made.)

> Scope and verification

All matching is exact byte equality. The trace owns original strings, actual
table, matches and comparison records; no second scan constructs its history.
Capture admission counts complete original bytes, table entries, tests and
output match identities, with a million-entry default and zero disabling only
the optional quota. It excludes private runtime copies, capacities and
bytes/RAM. Ordinary and count-only APIs retain no input/history and have no
optional capture ceiling.

Independent naive matching and direct border enumeration checked1000 byte-string
searches and37560 actual producing comparisons, including original byte
positions and fallback order. Another1000 binary searches/prefix tables matched
the frozen implementation exactly. Native tests additionally exhaust32193 binary
text/needle pairs, preserve overlaps and verify byte/NUL/high-byte domains,
complete capture admission and owned records. The ten-report shared build
passed141 native CTest cases,45 directly instrumented
address/undefined-behaviour sanitizer cases,90 compiled/executed public
examples,412/412 scoped file definitions plus11/11 changed lagged-Fibonacci
engine definitions, and ten representative clangd hovers. All four complete
report programs executed and all four native figures were visually reviewed.
Receipts and repeatable checks are retained under
`build/mepml-conversion/batch-184-193/`.

> References

D. E. Knuth, J. H. Morris, Jr., and V. R. Pratt(1977),
[Fast Pattern Matching in Strings|https://doi.org/10.1137/0206024], SIAM Journal
on Computing6(2),323–350. Native while-then-if tests and empty-needle
conventions are stated separately from the paper’s algorithmic complexity
result.
